        "text": "MICHEL MARTIN, HOST: Latino voters helped elect Republicans two years ago. A congressional race in south Texas is a test of whether that support holds. Republican Representative Monica De La Cruz is trying for a third term. Her challenger is Democrat Bobby Pulido, a singer, making his first run for office. Texas Public Radio's David Martin Davies takes us to the state's 15th District.",
